                                        <h3>The Trip Out to the Dive Site</h3>
                                        <p>The trip to the dive site is about 3 miles off the coast of Haleiwa and usually takes 20-30 minutes. During the trip, you'll be introduced to the crew and your safety divers and will be given a quick safety briefing covering what to expect, how to safely enter and exit the water (and the boat—important!), how to interact with the sharks, as well as how to use your snorkel gear.</p>
                                        
                                        <p>You'll have the opportunity to ask questions as well as site see since the trip includes scenic views of the north shore as well as the ocean open. It's not uncommon to see sea turtles, dolphins, or whales during whale season.</p>

                                        <p>This is a great time to talk to your photographer about your dive and what kind of shots and experience you'd like to have if you purchased tour photos or video.</p>

                                        <h3>The Dive</h3>
                                        <p>Once at the dive site and once the crew has determined that conditions are safe, you'll put on your snorkel gear and enter the water with the safety diver and other guests. Depending on the number of divers on the tour, there may be one or multiple safety divers.</p>

                                        <p>Once in the water, you'll have the opportunity to swim freely within the dive area which includes a safety rope.</p>
                                        <p>Divers that purchased a photo or video package will be diving with their photographer to capture photos and make the most out of available time.</p>

                                        <h3>Back to the Dock</h3>
                                        <p>After the dive, you'll make the trip back to the dock, get your land legs back, and have a new story to tell! Hopefully, one of many as you continue to enjoy the island and all it has to offer.</p>

